#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:107
msgid ""
"For a structured grid with dims (nx, ny, nz), there are only nx unique X "
"values, ny unique Y values, and nz unique Z values.  This class stores just "
"the unique values and expands them lazily when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:111
msgid "Repeat patterns (Fortran ordering, i fastest):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:112
msgid "Axis 0 (X): X[i] appears at indices where flat_idx % nx == i"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:113
msgid "Axis 1 (Y): Y[j] appears at indices where (flat_idx // nx) % ny == j"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:114
msgid "Axis 2 (Z): Z[k] appears at indices where flat_idx // (nx * ny) == k"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.numpy_interface.vtk_structured_point_array.md:106
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.numpy_interface.vtk_structured_point_array.md:279
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:110
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:112
msgid ""
"values : numpy array     The unique coordinate values for this axis. axis : "
"int     Which axis (0=X, 1=Y, 2=Z). dims : tuple of 3 ints     Grid "
"dimensions (nx, ny, nz). dataset : vtkDataObject, optional     The owning "
"dataset (kept as weak reference)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:162
msgid "Materialize the full 1D array using Fortran ordering (i fastest)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:170
msgid "Index into the array using Fortran ordering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:178
msgid "Handle numpy ufuncs.  Unary ufuncs and scalar operations stay lazy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.numpy_interface.vtk_structured_point_array.md:274
msgid ""
"Bases: {py:obj}`vtkmodules.numpy_interface._vtk_array_mixin."
"VTKDataArrayMixin`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:279
msgid ""
"Registered as an override for every ``vtkStructuredPointArray[dtype]`` "
"instantiation.  Every structured-point array returned by VTK (such as "
"``vtkImageData.points.data`` or ``vtkRectilinearGrid.points.data``) is an "
"instance of this class.  Ufunc and scalar results also come back as "
"instances of this class, built in-place via ``ConstructBackend``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:285
msgid ""
"Axis coordinates are read through the C++ ``GetXCoordinates()`` / "
"``GetYCoordinates()`` / ``GetZCoordinates()`` accessors so the wrapper stays "
"in lockstep with the backing array.  With an identity direction matrix (the "
"common case), indexing and ufuncs operate per-axis and stay lazy; reductions "
"use O(nx+ny+nz) formulas.  With a non-identity direction matrix, operations "
"fall back to a full materialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:291
msgid "Build a structured-point array from three 1D axis arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:293
msgid ""
"Picks a ``vtkStructuredPointArray[dtype]`` instantiation matching the input "
"axes' dtype, wraps the axes as VTK data arrays, and calls "
"``ConstructBackend`` to set up the lazy backend.  The returned array is an "
"instance of ``VTKStructuredPointArray`` (via the registered override) and "
"has identity direction matrix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:299
msgid "Get the X, Y, Z coordinate arrays directly from the backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:301
msgid ""
"Returns a list of 3 numpy arrays [X, Y, Z], or None if the backend has not "
"been constructed yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:307
msgid "Get grid dimensions from axis arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:315
msgid "Check if a non-identity direction matrix is being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:339
msgid "Materialize the full array as a numpy ndarray."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:341
msgid ""
"When axis arrays are available and no direction matrix is used, materializes "
"via meshgrid (efficient).  Otherwise, uses DeepCopy to an AOS array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:347
msgid "Return the full (N, 3) array as a numpy ndarray."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/numpy_interface/vtk_structured_point_array.py:579
msgid ""
"Templates that only have vtkType-based instantiations (e.g. vtkTypeFloat64) "
"need aliases under the native IA64 mangled names (e.g. _IdE for double) so "
"that the Python template subscript notation template['float64'] can find "
"them."
msgstr ""
